So season one, Greg asked me to dress up like Madonna in the background of a cutaway photo
第一季的时候，格雷格让我打扮成麦当娜，出现在一张插图照片的背景里，

166
00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:12.830
of Michael Scott and Dwight dressed as Crockett and Tubbs from Miami Vice at an 80s party.
照片里迈克尔·斯科特和德怀特打扮成《迈阿密风云》里的克罗克特和塔布斯，参加一场80年代派对。

167
00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.350
And I said yes.
我答应了。

168
00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:20.590
He asked me if I would do an insert shot for the fun run episode where I get hit by the car,
后来在慈善长跑那一集，他问我愿不愿意拍一个特写镜头，就是我被车撞的那场戏，

169
00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.210
where I actually hit the glass and roll off the top of the car and fall onto the ground
我真的撞到了挡风玻璃，从车顶滚下来，掉在地上，

170
00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.390
on a mat, but still.
虽然下面垫了垫子，但还是挺吓人的。

171
00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.010
And I said yes.
我也答应了。

172
00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:32.990
So Greg asked me if I'd shave my head, and I said, is there a plan B?
所以当格雷格问我愿不愿意剃光头时，我问他，有备选方案吗？

173
00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:35.090
And he said yes.
他说有。

174
00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:38.690
He said that plan B was a bald cap.
他说备选方案是戴光头套。

175
00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:44.070
So I said, it's a really big decision, so I'm going to sleep on it.
于是我说，这可是个重大决定，我得考虑一晚。

176
00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:50.750
So I emailed him first thing in the morning, and I said, I'd pick plan B.
第二天一早我就给他发了邮件，说我选备选方案。

177
00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.550
Plan B, too.
我也选备选方案。

178
00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.650
I'm very glad she picked plan B.
我很高兴她选了备选方案。

179
00:06:56.650 --> 00:07:02.070
I mean, she mentioned a few things, but she didn't even mention having a warehouse shelf
我是说，她提到了好几件事，但甚至都没提仓库货架

180
00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:02.870
fall on her.
砸在她身上的事。

181
00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:03.990
How about the bat?
那蝙蝠呢？

182
00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.430
The bat on her head?
蝙蝠落在她头上那次？

183
00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:08.470
The numerous flashing, yes.
还有无数次暴露身体，没错。

184
00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:14.210
I mean, Kate has shown up for this role in so many ways.
我是说，凯特为了这个角色真的付出了很多。

185
00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:18.150
I think it's A-OK that she said, I don't want to shave my head.
我觉得她说“我不想剃光头”完全没问题。

186
00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:18.450
Yeah.
是的。

187
00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:23.970
Well, Kate ended up getting the bald cap for this episode, and we asked her about what
总之，凯特最终在那一集里戴了光头套，我们问了她

188
00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.850
that process was like, and here is what she said.
那个过程是怎样的，她是这么说的。

189
00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:30.370
Ed French is like the greatest bald cap dude in the world.
埃德·弗伦奇是世界上最厉害的光头套大师。

190
00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.170
He teaches a lot of makeup artists how to do it.
他教过很多化妆师怎么做这个。

191
00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:36.690
He did the bald cap for Star Trek, the movie, from like, is that from 1980?
他给《星际迷航》电影做过光头套，那是1980年的吧？

192
00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:39.010
The bald lady, who's not really bald now.
那个光头女士，她现在其实不是光头。

193
00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:39.750
I didn't know that.
我以前不知道。

194
00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:40.330
I thought she was bald.
我还以为她是真光头。

195
00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:41.630
Ed did such a great job.
埃德做得太棒了。

196
00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:42.130
He's amazing.
他真是太厉害了。

197
00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:48.690
And the process for the full bald cap was every day for a week.
戴全套光头套的过程持续了一周，每天都要戴。

198
00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:53.870
Actually, technically, it was two weeks because there was another episode where I was wearing
其实严格来说是两周，因为还有另一集我需要戴

199
00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.270
a wig, it falls off, and I have a bald underneath.
假发，假发掉下来，下面露出光头。

200
00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.010
So we had two full weeks of this.
所以我们整整做了两周。

201
00:07:58.150 --> 00:07:58.450
Maybe not.
也许不是。

202
00:07:58.590 --> 00:07:59.550
No, maybe a week and a half.
不，也许要一个半星期。

203
00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:01.650
OK, it was awful.
好吧，那真是太糟糕了。

204
00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:02.210
No, it was great.
不，那很棒。

205
00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:02.870
It was fine.
还行吧。

206
00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:04.010
It was just a lot.
只是内容太多了。

207
00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:09.250
Three and a half hours in and two hours out, and they do this thing.
进去要三个半小时，出来要两个小时，而且他们还要做那种事。

208
00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:11.890
They literally sculpt your hair to fit your head.
他们真的是在雕刻你的头发，好让它贴合你的头型。

209
00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:16.450
They just, like, swirl it around, like, with this liquid that it just, it's crazy.
他们就是，怎么说呢，用一种液体把它绕起来，那感觉，太疯狂了。

210
00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.310
It's like a weird glue.
就像一种奇怪的胶水。

211
00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:20.530
It comes out, but it's like, whoa, it's intense.
虽然能洗掉，但那种感觉，哇，太强烈了。

212
00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:25.090
And then there's, like, wax, and there's, it's, and then he painted, like, blood vessels
然后还有蜡，还有，他甚至画上了血管，

213
00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:26.990
and, like, hair stubble.
还有胡茬。

214
00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:29.170
I mean, this guy was an artiSt.
我是说，这家伙真是个艺术家。

215
00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:30.130
Like, unbelievable.
简直不可思议。

216
00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:31.850
He's like the king daddy.
他可是大师中的大师。

217
00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.210
We would get there at 3.30 in the morning.
我们得在凌晨三点半赶到那里。

218
00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:37.710
You know, I was a little younger then, so whatever.
你知道，那时候我年轻一点，所以无所谓。

219
00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:38.370
Big whoop.
没什么大不了的。

220
00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:41.250
Three and a half hours.
三个半小时。

221
00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:43.610
And she had to get there at 3.30 in the morning.
她也得在凌晨三点半赶到那里。

222
00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.750
And then it takes two hours to get out of it.
而且卸妆还要花两个小时。

223
00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:52.610
And the glue and the wax and the, I mean, that is a, that is a journey, getting that bald cap on.
那些胶水、蜡，我是说，戴上那个秃头套真是一段漫长的旅程。

224
00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:58.130
So, you know, lady, years later, when I was on splitting up together, I had to get a bald cap.
所以，你知道，女士，多年后，当我在拍《分分合合》时，我也得戴秃头套。

225
00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.470
And it was the same guy.
而且还是同一个人。

226
00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:01.410
Ed French.
埃德·弗伦奇。

227
00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:02.770
He's the dude.
他才是大神。

228
00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:03.830
He's the guy.
就是他。

229
00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:06.590
He came and did this same process to me.
他过来对我做了同样的处理。

230
00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:10.350
And I remember reaching out to Kate and being like, guess who I'm with right now?
我记得我联系了凯特，说，猜猜我现在和谁在一起？

231
00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:11.630
Guess what's happening to me?
猜猜我正在经历什么？

232
00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:16.870
And also, she was, like, a person who knew what I was going through because she had done it.
而且，她也是个懂我感受的人，因为她也经历过。

233
00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:20.710
And she's like, doesn't your head get so cold when you get the, it is.
她说，戴上那个之后你的头不会觉得很冷吗？确实会。

234
00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.750
It's like, it's like a glue, but it's not glue.
那就像，就像胶水，但又不是胶水。

235
00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:37.350
But they have to put this stuff on your hair that, like, slicks it to your head so there's no bulges so that you have a perfectly round bald head when they put the bald cap on.
他们必须在你的头发上涂上这种东西，把它紧紧贴在头上，这样就不会有凸起，戴上秃头套后才能有一个圆润的秃头。

236
00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:42.250
But it's like, it takes so long because you have to do that, but then you have to wait.
但这太花时间了，因为你得做完那一步，然后还得等。

237
00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:44.530
And then you have to do the next step, and then you have to wait.
接着做下一步，然后还得等。

238
00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:53.790
And then he puts the bald cap on, and then there's all this airbrushing and, like, detail makeup to make it look seamless.
然后他戴上秃头套，再进行各种喷绘和细节化妆，让它看起来天衣无缝。

239
00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:55.410
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

240
00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:56.950
Here's the thing.
重点是这个。

241
00:09:57.130 --> 00:10:00.290
On splitting up together, they cut the scene.
在《分分合合》里，他们把那场戏剪掉了。

242
00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:01.550
Oh, no.
噢，不。

243
00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.890
You went through all of that, and they cut the scene?
你经历了这一切，结果他们把戏剪了？

244
00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:04.290
Yeah.
是啊。

245
00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:05.450
Can you even believe that?
你敢信吗？

246
00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:09.010
But anyway, I'll give you the pictures of me bald in my Ed French baldness.
不过没关系，我会给你看我戴着埃德·弗伦奇版秃头套的照片。

247
00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:10.590
Oh, I'll do a side-by-side.
噢，我要做一个对比图。

248
00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:15.450
You can do a side-by-side of me and Kate in our Ed French bald caps.
你可以把我和凯特戴着埃德·弗伦奇秃头套的照片放在一起对比。

249
00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:16.330
I love it.
我喜欢这个主意。

250
00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:18.350
Well, Kate, thank you so much.
好吧，凯特，非常感谢你。

251
00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:21.590
We're going to hear more from Kate as we break down this episode.
在解析这一集时，我们会听到更多凯特的分享。

252
00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:29.530
Moving on to fast fact number two, big guest star cameo alert, basketball legend, Dr.
接下来是第二个速览事实，大牌客串明星预警，篮球传奇，J博士。

253
00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:30.990
Julius Irving.
朱利叶斯·欧文。

254
00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.150
Dr. J in the house.
J博士驾到。

255
00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:44.850
For anyone who doesn't know, Dr. J won three NBA championships, four Most Valuable Player Awards, and three scoring titles with the Virginia Squires, New York Nets,
对于不知道的人，J博士曾随弗吉尼亚绅士队、纽约篮网队（也就是现在的布鲁克林篮网队）和费城76人队赢得了三次NBA总冠军、四次最有价值球员奖和三次得分王头衔，他是我们剧中的篮球传奇。

256
00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:52.310
who are now the Brooklyn Nets, and the Philadelphia 76ers, basketball legend on our show.
当你观看这一集时，如果你觉得天哪，吉姆这个角色在J博士面前太兴奋了，那其实就是约翰·卡拉辛斯基本人。

257
00:10:52.310 --> 00:11:00.490
When you watch this episode, if you think, gosh, the character Jim is so giddy around Dr. J, that is just John Krasinski.
他当时确实很兴奋。

258
00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.170
He was giddy.
他能参与那些场景拍摄感到非常开心。

259
00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.810
He was so tickled to be in those scenes.
嗯，安吉拉，我记得那件事。

260
00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:06.810
Well, Angela, I remember that.
所以我联系了约翰。

261
00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.450
So I reached out to John.
哦，是的。

262
00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:09.190
Oh, yeah.
他说了什么？

263
00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:09.790
What did he say?
我当时问他，约翰，关于和J博士合作，你有什么想说的吗？

264
00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:15.330
And I was like, John, do you have anything to say about working with Dr. J?
他是这么说的。

265
00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:16.970
And here's what he said.
他说，我的意思是，那可是J博士啊。

266
00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.430
He said, I mean, it was Dr. J.
我小时候墙上就贴着他的海报。

267
00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:23.770
Had a poster of him on my wall as a kid.
如果你告诉那个孩子，他有一天不仅会见到J博士，还能在电视节目中和他假装开商务会议。

268
00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:32.490
If you had told that kid that he would one day not only meet Dr. J, but pretend to have a fake business meeting with him on a television show.
还能和他一起投篮。

269
00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:35.150
And get to shoot a basket with him.
那个可怜的孩子估计会直接激动到晕过去。

270
00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.950
Well, that poor kid just blacked out.
是的，他太兴奋了。

271
00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:41.550
Yeah, he was so excited.
没错。

272
00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:42.190
Yeah.
太可爱了。

273
00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:43.370
It was so cute.
我觉得他在那些场景里根本不需要演。

274
00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.130
I don't think he had to act at all in those scenes.
一秒钟都不需要。

275
00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:45.970
Not for a second.
没错。

276
00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:46.250
No.
我们还收到了威廉·M发来的粉丝提问。

277
00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.370
We also got a fan question from William M.
来自，引用一下，美国空军的各个地方。

278
00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:53.030
from, quote, all over the United States Air Force.
你们是怎么请到J博士来演出的？

279
00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.530
How did you get Dr. J on the show?
嗯，威廉，NBC的高管之一劳伦·安德森是我们联系J博士的桥梁。

280
00:11:56.130 --> 00:12:02.270
Well, William, Lauren Anderson, who was one of the executives at NBC, was our connection to Dr. J.
好的。

281
00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:02.370
Okay.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，是她帮忙安排了他的出场。

282
00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:05.670
Steve Burgess told me she helped to arrange his appearance.
他那周只有一天有空。

283
00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:09.910
He was only available for one day that week.
他很忙。

284
00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:10.630
He's busy.
是的。

285
00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:11.230
Yeah.
我们安排他飞过来。

286
00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:12.690
We flew him in.
我们调整了整个拍摄计划，以便在那一天能请到他。

287
00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:16.450
We arranged our whole schedule so that we could have him for that one day.
太棒了。

288
00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:17.510
Amazing.
好了，珍娜，轮到你的第三个速览事实了。

289
00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.510
Well, Jenna, it's time for your Fast Fact number three.
我真的希望，你还没告诉我，但我真的希望这是关于虱子的深度解析。

290
00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:27.350
And I'm really hoping, you haven't told me, but I am really hoping that this is a deep dive on lice.
请告诉我就是这个。

291
00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.210
Please tell me it is.
女士，这可是梦想成真了。

292
00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:32.650
Lady, it is your dream come true.
我了解你吗？

293
00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:33.710
Do I know you?
我了解你。

294
00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:34.450
I know you.
我们现在都知道对方是怎么准备一集节目的了。

295
00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.870
We now know how each other preps an episode.
你懂的。

296
00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:37.870
You know it.
第三个速览事实是来自佐治亚州伍德斯托克的劳雷尔·M提供的虱子冷知识。

297
00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:42.670
Fast Fact three is lice trivia from Laurel M.
劳雷尔，你有什么发现？

298
00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.010
in Woodstock, Georgia.
劳雷尔是我们关于虱子的深度解析专家，因为她写给我们的信里是这么说的。

299
00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.950
Laurel, what do you have?
我们稍后会详细介绍。

300
00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:51.790
Laurel is our deep dive expert on lice because Laurel wrote us a letter that says this.
没错，这封信非常详尽。

301
00:12:52.030 --> 00:12:55.970
I am way more excited than I should be to write in about lice.
我写信来聊虱子，兴奋程度远超常理。

302
00:12:57.010 --> 00:13:08.590
However, seeing as that my family recently dealt with an infestation and my 12-year-old had to watch this episode while being lice-checked, I feel it's appropriate.
不过，鉴于我家最近刚闹过虱子，我12岁的孩子在检查虱子时还得看这集节目，我觉得这很应景。

303
00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:10.790
Here is what Laurel had to say.
以下是劳雷尔（Laurel）想说的内容。

304
00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.830
Lice Fast Facts.
虱子速查事实。

305
00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:16.670
One, lice-like clean scalps.
第一，虱子喜欢干净的头皮。

306
00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:18.910
Clean scalps.
干净的头皮。

307
00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:19.310
Yes.
没错。

308
00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:24.390
So in this episode, we're assuming that it was like, oh, Meredith never bathes.
所以这集里，我们以为是因为，噢，梅雷迪思（Meredith）从不洗澡。

