1255
00:51:50.410 --> 00:51:56.590
Oh, well, Kate sent us in an audio clip sharing all about this, and you got to hear it.
噢，凯特给我们发了一段音频，分享了这一切，你们一定要听听。

1256
00:51:57.510 --> 00:52:03.570
How that all worked, all the scenes worked, especially the one where I'm specifically shaving my head, like where you actually see it.
关于这一切是如何运作的，所有的场景是如何拍摄的，尤其是那个我剃头的镜头，就是你们真正看到的那一幕。

1257
00:52:04.310 --> 00:52:09.770
Yeah, it took like three and a half hours to get into the bald cap with a partial wig for that scene.
是的，为了那个镜头，光是戴上秃头套和部分假发就花了三个半小时。

1258
00:52:09.770 --> 00:52:11.870
So I look like Benjamin Franklin.
所以我看起来像本杰明·富兰克林。

1259
00:52:12.210 --> 00:52:15.670
And then they had me put hair in my hand.
然后他们让我把头发放在手里。

1260
00:52:15.670 --> 00:52:20.590
Like I actually had my hand on top of my head holding the extra hair so you couldn't tell.
就像我真的把手放在头顶上抓着多余的头发，这样你就看不出来了。

1261
00:52:20.850 --> 00:52:21.850
It was a pretty quick shot.
那是一个相当快的镜头。

1262
00:52:22.030 --> 00:52:29.430
And then I had the razor in my right hand, hair on top of my head with my left hand, and then I just rolled it over and just like let the hair drop.
当时我右手拿着剃刀，左手抓着头顶的头发，然后我只是把它翻过来，让头发掉下来。

1263
00:52:29.630 --> 00:52:32.390
So a little movie magic when I said, what does it look like?
所以当我问“看起来怎么样？”的时候，那其实是电影魔术。

1264
00:52:32.470 --> 00:52:33.110
I'm baking a cake.
我在烤蛋糕。

1265
00:52:33.790 --> 00:52:36.790
God, I think I said it funnier right just then than I did at the time.
天哪，我觉得我刚才说得比当时还要好笑。

1266
00:52:36.930 --> 00:52:38.610
Anyway, so that was kind of cool.
总之，那挺酷的。

1267
00:52:38.610 --> 00:52:39.830
It was like a cool little illusion.
就像一个很酷的小把戏。

1268
00:52:40.650 --> 00:52:42.350
And I can say that is how we did it.
我可以告诉你们我们就是这样做的。

1269
00:52:42.430 --> 00:52:42.850
I remember.
我记得。

1270
00:52:43.010 --> 00:52:44.090
It was not easy, though.
不过这并不容易。

1271
00:52:44.270 --> 00:52:48.150
It was very hard because she had so much business to do, you know?
这非常难，因为她当时要处理的事情太多了，你懂吗？

1272
00:52:48.370 --> 00:52:55.270
Like she had to hold fake hair in one hand, a razor in another hand, kind of like make it all fall out.
她得一只手拿着假发，另一只手拿着剃刀，还得让头发全部掉下来。

1273
00:52:55.390 --> 00:52:59.470
She had to do that whole illusion while acting and the timing and the microwave.
她必须在演戏的同时完成整个幻觉动作，还要把握好时机和微波炉的戏份。

1274
00:52:59.850 --> 00:53:04.390
I thought she did a great job because it really looks like her hair is just cascading down.
我觉得她做得非常棒，因为看起来真的就像她的头发在倾泻而下。

1275
00:53:04.510 --> 00:53:04.730
Yes.
是的。

1276
00:53:04.890 --> 00:53:06.890
Not that she's holding it and letting it go.
而不是她抓着头发然后松开。

1277
00:53:07.430 --> 00:53:11.770
And this is what they practiced that Monday, the first day that we filmed.
这就是他们在那周一，也就是我们拍摄的第一天练习的内容。

1278
00:53:11.970 --> 00:53:12.110
Yeah.
没错。

1279
00:53:12.390 --> 00:53:14.010
To make sure that it would look realistic.
为了确保它看起来足够真实。

1280
00:53:14.910 --> 00:53:20.650
Pam has a talking head now where she says, listen, I'm going to tell her, but now is clearly not the time.
帕姆现在有一个采访镜头，她说，听着，我会告诉她的，但显然现在不是时候。

1281
00:53:21.190 --> 00:53:21.430
Yeah.
嗯。

1282
00:53:21.430 --> 00:53:22.570
I'll buy her a wig.
我会给她买顶假发。

1283
00:53:22.570 --> 00:53:24.090
We'll laugh about it later.
我们以后会拿这件事开玩笑的。

1284
00:53:24.990 --> 00:53:25.970
Oh, Pam.
噢，帕姆。

1285
00:53:26.150 --> 00:53:27.670
Pam still hasn't told her.
帕姆还是没告诉她。

1286
00:53:27.890 --> 00:53:28.950
Pam, Pam, Pam.
帕姆，帕姆，帕姆。

1287
00:53:29.270 --> 00:53:29.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1288
00:53:30.150 --> 00:53:34.270
In the conference room, Dwight is running a meeting about lice.
在会议室里，德怀特正在主持一场关于虱子的会议。

1289
00:53:34.490 --> 00:53:38.570
And there's a big gross picture of a giant lice bug.
还有一张巨大的、恶心的虱子特写照片。

1290
00:53:38.830 --> 00:53:39.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1291
00:53:39.190 --> 00:53:43.610
And Erin is going to tell everyone they need mayonnaise to suffocate the lice.
艾琳告诉大家，他们需要蛋黄酱来闷死虱子。

1292
00:53:43.610 --> 00:53:47.750
They're going to need to pick a partner, and they're going to put mayonnaise on each other's head.
他们需要找个搭档，然后互相在对方头上涂抹蛋黄酱。

1293
00:53:48.210 --> 00:53:48.530
Yes.
是的。

1294
00:53:49.090 --> 00:53:50.790
Meredith arrives to the meeting.
梅雷迪思来到了会议现场。

1295
00:53:51.250 --> 00:53:54.350
This is when she reveals her full bald head.
就在这时，她露出了她完全光秃的头。

1296
00:53:54.530 --> 00:53:54.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1297
00:53:55.070 --> 00:53:59.090
She says she's the only one with the balls to show the lice who's boss.
她说她是唯一有胆量向虱子展示谁才是老大的人。

1298
00:53:59.410 --> 00:53:59.930
Yes.
没错。

1299
00:53:59.930 --> 00:54:03.630
We had a fan question from Emmeline C.
我们收到了一位来自比利时的粉丝艾米琳·C的提问。

1300
00:54:03.830 --> 00:54:09.210
in Belgian who said, this episode has my favorite Angela line of the whole series.
她说，这一集有我整部剧里最喜欢的安吉拉台词。

1301
00:54:09.570 --> 00:54:10.490
Really, Emmeline?
真的吗，艾米琳？

1302
00:54:10.790 --> 00:54:11.190
Yes.
是的。

1303
00:54:11.430 --> 00:54:14.450
After Meredith shaves her head, she says to the office, take a picture.
梅雷迪思剃光头后，她对办公室的人说，拍张照吧。

1304
00:54:14.570 --> 00:54:15.450
It'll last longer.
这样能留得久一点。

1305
00:54:15.610 --> 00:54:18.170
And Angela replies, we don't want it to last longer.
安吉拉回了一句，我们可不想让它留得久一点。

1306
00:54:18.170 --> 00:54:18.910
It's horrible.
太可怕了。

1307
00:54:19.950 --> 00:54:23.050
Everything about Angela's delivery makes me laugh so hard.
安吉拉说这句台词的方式总是让我笑得不行。

1308
00:54:23.270 --> 00:54:24.810
Was this line scripted?
这句台词是剧本里写的吗？

1309
00:54:24.910 --> 00:54:26.850
And if so, what did the script say exactly?
如果是的话，剧本里到底是怎么写的？

1310
00:54:26.890 --> 00:54:29.350
Were there any candy bag alts for this scene?
这场戏有没有其他的备选台词？

1311
00:54:29.350 --> 00:54:30.510
Please tell me everything.
请把一切都告诉我。

1312
00:54:30.810 --> 00:54:31.910
It was scripted.
这是剧本里写的。

1313
00:54:32.010 --> 00:54:37.690
I delivered it exactly as it was written, and I really loved all of Angela's reactions to Meredith.
我完全照着剧本念的，我真的很喜欢安吉拉对梅雷迪思的所有反应。

1314
00:54:37.970 --> 00:54:41.090
So, Emmeline, thank you for noting that.
所以，艾米琳，谢谢你注意到这一点。

1315
00:54:41.450 --> 00:54:43.990
There's one coming up where I'm like, are you happy, Pam?
接下来还有一场戏，我说的是，你开心了吗，帕姆？

1316
00:54:44.130 --> 00:54:45.050
She's a monster.
她真是个怪物。

1317
00:54:45.290 --> 00:54:46.230
Yes, I know.
是的，我知道。

1318
00:54:47.070 --> 00:54:48.450
I love that, too.
我也很喜欢那一段。

1319
00:54:49.230 --> 00:54:51.970
Pam is going to offer to go and get the mayonnaise.
帕姆主动提出要去拿蛋黄酱。

1320
00:54:52.510 --> 00:54:52.690
Yeah.
没错。

1321
00:54:53.070 --> 00:54:53.970
She's like, I'll get it.
她说，我去拿吧。

1322
00:54:54.070 --> 00:54:55.070
I'll go get the mayo.
我去拿蛋黄酱。

1323
00:54:55.310 --> 00:54:56.390
Because she's feeling guilty.
因为她感到内疚。

1324
00:54:56.730 --> 00:54:57.650
She is.
确实是。

1325
00:54:58.130 --> 00:55:03.670
In the warehouse, we've got Daryl, Kevin, Phyllis, and Nellie all sitting around a table.
在仓库里，达里尔、凯文、菲利斯和内莉都坐在桌子旁。

1326
00:55:04.090 --> 00:55:05.090
They're working.
他们在工作。

1327
00:55:05.470 --> 00:55:10.010
And Val says hi to Daryl, and it's just like, oh, my gosh.
瓦尔跟达里尔打招呼，那种感觉，天哪。

1328
00:55:10.490 --> 00:55:11.330
Look at that.
看看那个场面。

1329
00:55:11.430 --> 00:55:13.350
Nellie is like, it's like a car crash.
内莉说，就像车祸现场一样。

1330
00:55:14.270 --> 00:55:15.230
So awkward.
太尴尬了。

1331
00:55:15.810 --> 00:55:18.170
Phyllis asks Daryl, what would make you feel better?
菲利斯问达里尔，什么能让你感觉好点？

1332
00:55:18.270 --> 00:55:21.470
And he was like, maybe chocolate cake, like my grandmother used to make.
他说，也许是像我祖母以前做的那种巧克力蛋糕。

1333
00:55:21.950 --> 00:55:22.850
And he gets up.
然后他站了起来。

1334
00:55:22.910 --> 00:55:24.890
He says, I need a minute to clear my head.
他说，我需要一点时间清醒一下。

1335
00:55:25.570 --> 00:55:28.010
Kevin thinks he could use some hugs and chocolate cake.
凯文觉得他可能需要拥抱和巧克力蛋糕。

1336
00:55:28.150 --> 00:55:32.110
And I loved when Phyllis gets really defensive about her chocolate muffin.
我很喜欢菲利斯为了她的巧克力松饼变得非常防备的样子。

1337
00:55:32.270 --> 00:55:33.070
She's like, this is not.
她说，这不是。

1338
00:55:33.370 --> 00:55:34.390
This wouldn't do it.
这个没用。

1339
00:55:34.410 --> 00:55:35.650
No, because it's not cake.
没错，因为它不是蛋糕。

1340
00:55:35.810 --> 00:55:36.110
No.
不是。

1341
00:55:36.270 --> 00:55:37.150
It's just a muffin.
它只是个松饼。

1342
00:55:37.450 --> 00:55:38.210
Made me laugh.
把我逗笑了。

1343
00:55:39.430 --> 00:55:40.030
All right.
好了。

1344
00:55:40.130 --> 00:55:42.850
Now we're headed over to Jim's big meeting.
现在我们要去吉姆的重要会议了。

1345
00:55:43.490 --> 00:55:47.910
He and Dr. J, they are shooting baskets.
他和J博士正在投篮。

1346
00:55:48.290 --> 00:55:48.510
Yeah.
没错。

1347
00:55:49.090 --> 00:55:50.390
Nothing but net, Halpert.
空心入网，哈尔珀特。

1348
00:55:50.910 --> 00:55:51.510
Amazing.
太棒了。

1349
00:55:52.090 --> 00:55:53.790
Pam is going to call Jim.
帕姆要给吉姆打电话。

1350
00:55:54.270 --> 00:56:01.230
She's unloading a bunch of mayonnaise from the car, and it's falling at her feet and exploding.
她正从车里卸下一堆蛋黄酱，结果掉在脚边炸开了。

1351
00:56:01.470 --> 00:56:02.810
Those were real mayonnaise jars.
那些真的是蛋黄酱罐子。

1352
00:56:03.190 --> 00:56:09.170
I really have a lot of fun doing scenes where I get to drop things and be like fumbly.
我真的很喜欢拍那些需要我把东西掉在地上、表现得笨手笨脚的戏。

1353
00:56:09.410 --> 00:56:09.650
Okay.
好吧。

1354
00:56:09.790 --> 00:56:10.430
Good to know.
知道了。

1355
00:56:10.530 --> 00:56:11.170
I love club.
我喜欢俱乐部。

1356
00:56:11.170 --> 00:56:12.950
Mom detectives, you're the klutz.
妈妈侦探，你才是那个笨手笨脚的人。

1357
00:56:13.090 --> 00:56:13.810
I'm the klutz.
我是那个笨手笨脚的人。

1358
00:56:13.910 --> 00:56:17.610
Oh, when we have our own show, I get to do klutzy things all the time.
噢，等我们有了自己的节目，我就能一直做那些笨手笨脚的事了。

1359
00:56:17.610 --> 00:56:19.390
You're the klutz and mom detectives.
你是那个笨手笨脚的妈妈侦探。

1360
00:56:19.550 --> 00:56:24.550
Lady, remember our movie that we wrote had me falling over that fence.
女士，记得我们写的那个电影剧本里，我翻过那道栅栏吗。

1361
00:56:24.790 --> 00:56:25.190
Yes.
记得。

1362
00:56:25.410 --> 00:56:28.470
You're so excited to do some stunt moment.
你对做特技动作感到非常兴奋。

1363
00:56:28.610 --> 00:56:29.970
I love to do that bit.
我喜欢做那个桥段。

1364
00:56:29.970 --> 00:56:30.910
I don't know why.
我也不知道为什么。

1365
00:56:31.250 --> 00:56:35.250
So I hope you liked my mayo dropping because I enjoyed doing it.
所以我希望你喜欢我掉蛋黄酱的那一幕，因为我拍得很开心。

1366
00:56:35.250 --> 00:56:36.410
I thought you did a great job.
我觉得你演得很棒。

1367
00:56:36.550 --> 00:56:37.590
It splattered perfectly.
溅开的效果非常完美。

1368
00:56:37.890 --> 00:56:38.150
It did.
确实。

1369
00:56:38.150 --> 00:56:42.910
And once again, in this Jim and Pam phone conversation, neither of them are really sharing
再说回吉姆和帕姆的这次通话，他们俩其实都没有分享

1370
00:56:42.910 --> 00:56:43.530
what's happening.
正在发生的事情。

1371
00:56:43.710 --> 00:56:47.770
Pam is not telling him that the whole entire office is about to put mayonnaise on their
帕姆没有告诉他，整个办公室的人马上就要把蛋黄酱涂在

1372
00:56:47.770 --> 00:56:48.110
heads.
头上了。

1373
00:56:48.390 --> 00:56:53.430
Jim isn't sharing that he's drinking a fresh made smoothie and shooting baskets with Dr.
吉姆也没有分享他正在喝新鲜果昔，还和J博士

1374
00:56:53.530 --> 00:56:53.690
J.
一起投篮。

1375
00:56:53.890 --> 00:56:56.970
And even Dr. J is going to give him a pair of Japanese Nikes.
甚至J博士还要送他一双日本产的耐克鞋。

1376
00:56:57.390 --> 00:56:57.850
I know.
我知道。

1377
00:56:57.850 --> 00:57:05.270
You know, that Nike joke is very funny because I guess maybe I remembered this when I was
你知道吗，那个耐克的笑话很有趣，因为我想我在看这集的时候

1378
00:57:05.270 --> 00:57:05.750
watching the episode.
可能记住了这一点。

1379
00:57:05.890 --> 00:57:06.530
I was like, Nikes?
我当时想，耐克？

1380
00:57:06.850 --> 00:57:07.970
Dr. J didn't wear Nikes?
J博士不是穿耐克的吗？

1381
00:57:08.830 --> 00:57:09.590
What is that?
那是什么？

1382
00:57:09.690 --> 00:57:10.190
What was that?
那是什么意思？

1383
00:57:10.290 --> 00:57:12.070
Was that meant to be like an extra joke?
那是为了增加一个额外的笑话吗？

1384
00:57:12.290 --> 00:57:14.410
Because Dr. J wore Converse.
因为J博士穿的是匡威。

1385
00:57:14.790 --> 00:57:20.030
He like made the Converse pro leather famous like back in the 1970s.
他在70年代让匡威的专业皮质运动鞋变得很有名。

1386
00:57:20.030 --> 00:57:25.430
It was like a big thing where like, you know, athletes are suddenly now making like shoes
当时这可是件大事，你知道，运动员突然开始让某种鞋子

1387
00:57:25.430 --> 00:57:27.310
or clothing like kind of famous.
或服装变得出名了。

1388
00:57:27.510 --> 00:57:28.250
I like totally remember that.
我完全记得这件事。

1389
00:57:28.330 --> 00:57:31.030
I was very proud of myself because I don't know a lot about sports, but I did remember
我当时对自己感到很自豪，因为我对体育了解不多，但我确实记得

1390
00:57:31.030 --> 00:57:31.310
that.
那件事。

1391
00:57:31.550 --> 00:57:34.110
Is it because you watched a movie and it was in the movie?
是因为你看过一部电影，里面提到了吗？

1392
00:57:34.330 --> 00:57:36.610
No, I didn't watch that basketball thing.
不，我没看过那个篮球节目。

1393
00:57:36.770 --> 00:57:37.450
I didn't watch it.
我没看。

1394
00:57:37.590 --> 00:57:38.630
Lee watched it.
李看了。

1395
00:57:38.710 --> 00:57:39.390
I didn't watch that.
我没看那个。

1396
00:57:39.990 --> 00:57:44.230
No, I just remembered it wasn't Nike that was a different shoe.
不，我只是记得那不是耐克，是另一种鞋。

1397
00:57:44.610 --> 00:57:45.050
I don't know.
我不知道。

1398
00:57:45.190 --> 00:57:47.210
I had to look up what shoe, I confess.
我承认，我不得不去查了查到底是哪种鞋。

1399
00:57:47.610 --> 00:57:49.310
But I do remember it wasn't Nike.
但我确实记得那不是耐克。

1400
00:57:50.030 --> 00:57:55.790
But then the other thing, Angela, that this made me think of about like athletes and clothing
但还有一件事，安吉拉，这让我想到了关于运动员和服装的话题

1401
00:57:55.790 --> 00:58:00.850
and stuff is the current, oh my gosh, I feel self-conscious because I've had so many side
还有那些乱七八糟的，天哪，我感觉有点不自在，因为我今天说了太多

1402
00:58:00.850 --> 00:58:01.430
stories today.
题外话了。

1403
00:58:01.570 --> 00:58:04.310
I don't know if I'm just excited because you celebrated my birthday and I'm being real
我不知道是因为你给我庆祝生日让我太兴奋了，还是我本来就这么

1404
00:58:04.310 --> 00:58:04.750
chatty.
爱唠叨。

1405
00:58:04.890 --> 00:58:06.670
And you've had a nice big piece of cake.
